tic","verb":"edit","decisions":[]},{"id":"1791044408.798761-edit","invocation":{"verb":"edit","args":{"before":"`A.equality('trivia').eq(a, b, spec)` / `.hash(t, spec)` with `spec = require('cartograph.algebraread').trivia('lua')` — the adapter's TRIVIA, derived not listed: the node types the PARSER reported as extras (tree-sitter's grammar-declared extras: `comment`) + the gap rule (a whitespace-only literal); `A.strip_trivia(t, spec)` drops them (unchanged subtrees shared). A spec is required — never guessed.","after":"`A.equality('trivia').eq(a, b)` / `.hash(t)` — the TRIVIA the reader MARKED on each occurrence as it read the code (`trivia = true`, not identity): every GAP it keeps between tokens and around the root, and every node the PARSER reports as an extra (tree-sitter's grammar-declared extras: comments) — derived per occurrence, so the answer is a function of the term alone, and whitespace INSIDE a token (`\" \"` vs `\"  \"`) is content, never trivia; `A.strip_trivia(t)` drops the marked occurrences (unchanged subtrees shared).","file":".claude/skills/cartograph/references/questions.md"},"touched":[".claude/skills/cartograph/references/questions.md"]},"bytes":1136,"decided_by":"tactic","verb":"edit","decisions":[]}],"hand":0}
